<h2 class="bde-heading-1944-123 bde-heading">
Start With the Right Measure</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-1944-124 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<p class="bde-f-text-1944-152 bde-f-text">
Salary
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-153 bde-f-text">
The player’s listed pay for a season. The label states whether a table uses base salary or a wider cash measure.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-154 bde-f-text">
Cap hit
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-155 bde-f-text">
The amount counted against the salary cap under the applicable accounting rules. It can differ from the player’s cash salary.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-156 bde-f-text">
Guaranteed money
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-157 bde-f-text">
Money protected under the terms of the contract. Partial guarantees, trigger dates and conditional protection need separate treatment.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-158 bde-f-text">
Scheduled dollars
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-159 bde-f-text">
Amounts listed for future contract seasons. Options and non-guaranteed years are identified; the total is not necessarily guaranteed spending.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-160 bde-f-text">
Cap holds
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-161 bde-f-text">
Accounting amounts that preserve certain rights or reserve cap space. They are not signed player salaries.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-162 bde-f-text">
Luxury tax &amp; aprons
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-163 bde-f-text">
The tax threshold and the first and second aprons are different benchmarks. Tax estimates and apron comparisons use the relevant salary measure rather than assuming active payroll answers every question.
</p>
</div>
</div><div id="calculations" class="bde-fancy-container-1944-107 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h2 class="bde-heading-1944-125 bde-heading">
How We Calculate Comparisons</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-1944-126 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-1944-164 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h3 class="bde-heading-1944-168 bde-heading">
Percentage of the Cap
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-1944-169 bde-f-text">
Player cap hit ÷ the salary cap for that season × 100. Team comparisons use the stated team salary measure and the same season’s cap.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-1944-165 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h3 class="bde-heading-1944-170 bde-heading">
Percentage of Payroll
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-1944-171 bde-f-text">
Player salary measure ÷ the corresponding roster total × 100. Cash salary and cap hit are kept on a consistent basis within a comparison.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-1944-166 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h3 class="bde-heading-1944-172 bde-heading">
Season-To-Season Change
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-1944-173 bde-f-text">
Current season minus previous season. Dollar changes show + or −. Changes in a cap percentage are shown in percentage points, not as percentage growth.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-1944-167 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h3 class="bde-heading-1944-174 bde-heading">
League Rankings
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-1944-175 bde-f-text">
Teams are compared within the same season and salary definition. Future-year rankings include only teams with usable figures for that year; the coverage count belongs alongside the rank.
</p>
</div>
</div><p class="bde-f-text-1944-127 bde-f-text">
Dollar amounts are in US dollars. Compact labels may be rounded; totals and calculations should use the underlying figures.
</p>
</div><div id="contracts" class="bde-fancy-container-1944-108 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h2 class="bde-heading-1944-128 bde-heading">
History Follows the Contracts</h2><p class="bde-f-text-1944-129 bde-f-text">
Player history is organized around contracts, extensions and other meaningful changes in employment terms. A long career with one franchise can contain several distinct contract periods.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-130 bde-f-text">
Annual figures remain available within those periods. An extension signing date and the first season it takes effect are separate facts. We avoid counting the same salary twice when a new agreement overlaps an existing deal.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-131 bde-f-text">
Options and guarantee conditions stay attached to the relevant season. An option year is not automatically treated as an exercised year.
</p>
</div><div id="research" class="bde-fancy-container-1944-109 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h2 class="bde-heading-1944-132 bde-heading">
Research and Updates</h2><p class="bde-f-text-1944-133 bde-f-text">
Our research draws on league and team announcements, contract records, established salary databases and reporting that identifies the relevant terms. Financial records are reconciled by player, team and season.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-134 bde-f-text">
Pages carry research dates where available. A research date describes the snapshot behind the figures; it does not imply that every figure updates in real time.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1944-135 bde-f-text">
When a material detail cannot be established, we leave it unconfirmed. A blank amount does not mean zero. We retain supporting references so figures can be checked and corrected.
</p>
</div><div id="estimates" class="bde-fancy-container-1944-110 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h2 class="bde-heading-1944-136 bde-heading">
Estimates Need Context</h2><h3 class="bde-heading-1944-137 bde-heading">
Net Worth
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-1944-138 bde-f-text">
Net worth estimates describe an estimated balance of assets and liabilities. They are not verified account balances, and career salary is not a substitute for net worth. Taxes, spending, investments, endorsements and liabilities can all change the picture.
</p><h3 class="bde-heading-1944-139 bde-heading">
Tax Bills and Future Seasons
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-1944-140 bde-f-text">
Projected tax bills depend on the relevant taxable salary, the season’s tax bands and the team’s repeater status. A projection is not a confirmed payment. Future payroll can change through options, guarantees, trades, waivers and new contracts.
</p><h3 class="bde-heading-1944-141 bde-heading">
Historical Comparisons
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-1944-142 bde-f-text">
Historical dollar figures are nominal unless stated otherwise. Payroll as a percentage of that season’s cap provides additional context without presenting it as an inflation adjustment.
</p>
</div><div id="corrections" class="bde-fancy-container-1944-111 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h2 class="bde-heading-1944-143 bde-heading">
Help Us Improve the Record</h2><p class="bde-f-text-1944-144 bde-f-text">
If something looks wrong, send the page, season and detail to check. A supporting link is welcome. Corrections should update the affected figure and any calculations that depend on it.
</p><div class="bde-button-1944-145 bde-button">
        
    
    
    
    
            
                    
            
            

    
    
    
    
    
